Burnaston plant – produced by Toyota Auris and Avensis – produced almost 150 000 cars last year, 90% of which were exported to the remainder of the European Union.
"It is my stance that if Britain comes out without a deal at the end of March, we will experience production stalemases at our factory," said Marvin Cooke, Toyotin's director-general at Burnaston.
