"Eventions not only of Toyote but other manufacturers show that we must absolutely be able to continue this very successful series of supply chains."
At Toyota, they couldn't say how long production could be halted, but they warned that in the long-term, additional costs would reduce the factory's competitiveness and eventually lead to job losses.
