The Scottish government has already pledged to cover the costs of applying for EU citizens working in its decentralised public services.
Ms Freeman wrote: "During the summer, negotiations between the United Kingdom and the European Union on Withdrawal have resumed, which are moving towards expected decisions this autumn.
But the U.S. government is also stepplining preparations for a no-deal scenario.
I'm sure it's a very difficult period for all of you.
That's why I'd now like to point out again how much I appreciate the contribution of every staff member, regardless of their nationality.
