And this entails fixing our deteriorating housing market.
Britain will always be open to people who want to live, work and build their lives here.
However, it can't be right that individuals who don't live in the United Kingdom, as well as companies established abroad, can buy homes as easily as hard-working Britons.
“The dream of owning a home to a large number of people has gone too far, and the embarrassment of homelessness remains very real.”
